The '''Armed Forces of Sinchew''' are the military of the state, comprising the '''army''', the '''navy''' and the '''ranger corps'''.

They were established as a standing professional force by the [[Constitution of Sinchew]] of 1733, and they are subordinate to the [[General Assembly of Sinchew|General Assembly]], which raises, funds and directs them. The constitution vests the conduct of foreign affairs in the president and the power to raise and commit the forces in the Assembly, so that no commander may engage the state in a war.

== Army ==

The army is the land force.

== Navy ==

The navy is the maritime force, and is the successor to the naval tradition of the colony, which had been a possession of [[Zong]] and whose officers had served in the imperial fleets.

== Rangers ==

The rangers are the force responsible for the interior, and are the reason the state maintains three services rather than two.

Their task is the maintenance of order in the hinterlands and the forests of the country, and they are trained to traverse mountain and jungle and to operate in small units in difficult country. They are constituted as commando units, and the corps is the instrument by which the republic governs territory that has no civil administration.

The corps exists because of the shape of the country. The republic inherited two large provinces containing chiefdoms that had never been subject to the colony: [[Hashawa]], of 685,898 km², and [[Ytyba]], of 221,029 km². Together they hold 906,927 km², or 44.8 per cent of the national territory, and about 209,600 people, or 6.1 per cent of the population. Two of the sixteen provinces contain nearly half the country and govern almost none of it, and the ranger corps is the instrument by which the state reaches them. The rangers are the force that operates in them, and their duties are as much civil as military.

== Command ==

The president is the civilian commander of the armed forces. The office holds no domestic executive power under the constitution, and the command of the military is the third of its functions alongside the conduct of foreign affairs and the administration of the Assembly's agencies.

The arrangement places the forces under a civilian authority that is itself appointed by the [[General Assembly of Sinchew|General Assembly]], which raises, funds and may direct them. The president commands and the Assembly decides, so that the officer corps is not in the position the colonial navy occupied in 1711, when an admiral at [[Tamsui]] began a war on his own authority.

